---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { SECTIONS } from "../data/sections";

const title = "How Much Does a Used Treadmill Cost? (2026): Prices by Brand";
const description =
  "A used Peloton Tread typically sold for about $1,800 and remanufactured gym treadmills cost $3,799 to $10,599 (Nov 2026). Dated used vs new prices by brand.";

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "By Price", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/price/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "How Much Does a Used Treadmill Cost?", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/how-much-does-a-used-treadmill-cost/" },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How much does a used treadmill cost?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "It depends on the seller. On 25 November 2026 remanufactured gym treadmills cost $3,799 to $10,599 at one specialist dealer, maker scratch-and-dent curved trainers sold at about 87% of new, and a resale marketplace put a typical used Peloton Tread sale at about $1,800 in August 2026. Private-sale prices vary too much to quote; price-check them against comparable listings and new sale prices.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What percentage of the new price should I pay for a used treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "There is no reliable single percentage. In the dated pairs we found, maker seconds were about 87% of new, remanufactured commercial machines 43% to 59% of a new commercial price, and used Peloton treadmills roughly half the list price of their replacements. For a private sale, start from the new sale price and subtract moving, needed parts and the missing warranty.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How much is a used Peloton Tread worth?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Commonplace, a resale marketplace, reported a typical used Tread sale of about $1,800 (median $1,786) in August 2026 and a median asking price of $2,157.50 on 7 October. A new Tread Flex was $1,995 at Peloton on 24 November 2026, so a used Tread needs to sit clearly below that once activation and delivery are added.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Are refurbished treadmills worth it?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "They can be, when the refurbisher states what was replaced and gives a written warranty. Fitness Superstore, for example, includes a 1-year parts and on-site labour warranty on its remanufactured treadmills. Compare the price against a new machine on sale, not against its list price.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How many hours is too many on a used treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Our checklist treats under 500 hours on a home machine as light use and over 1,500 hours as approaching mid-life; commercial machines are built for far more. Maintenance matters more than hours, so ask when the deck was last lubricated.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is it cheaper to buy a used treadmill or a new one on Black Friday?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Below about $1,000 new, the Black Friday price usually wins once you count delivery, a likely belt and the warranty you would lose. Used makes more sense for mid-range and commercial machines you can collect yourself, or for remanufactured machines sold with a warranty.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", "@id": "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#shaheer-ali-khan", name: "Shaheer Ali Khan", honorificSuffix: "PhD", jobTitle: "Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist", url: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#who", sameAs: ["https://www.linkedin.com/in/shaheer-ali-khan-data/"], worksFor: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" } },
      datePublished: "2026-11-25",
      dateModified: "2026-11-27",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" },
    },
  ],
};

// "More in" links: the other pages in this article's hub group.
const HERE = "/how-much-does-a-used-treadmill-cost/";
const HUB = SECTIONS.find((s) => s.slug === "price");
const GROUP = HUB?.groups.find((g) => g.pages.some((p) => p.url === HERE)) ?? HUB?.groups[0];
const GROUP_PAGES = GROUP?.pages ?? [];
const HERE_AT = GROUP_PAGES.findIndex((p) => p.url === HERE);
// The group's first 2 pages (its leads), then the pages after this one, wrapping round, so every page in a long
// hub group gets sibling links and the leads keep theirs (PLAYBOOK §0b L1).
const MORE = [...new Set([...GROUP_PAGES.slice(0, 2), ...GROUP_PAGES.slice(HERE_AT + 1), ...GROUP_PAGES.slice(0, Math.max(HERE_AT, 0))])].filter((p) => p.url !== HERE).slice(0, 6);
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} | Treadmill Reviews USA`}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: "2026-11-25",
    modifiedTime: "2026-11-27",
    author: "Shaheer Ali Khan",
    section: "Fitness Equipment",
    tags: [
      "how much does a used treadmill cost",
      "used treadmill price",
      "used treadmill cost",
      "refurbished treadmill price",
      "remanufactured treadmill price",
      "used peloton tread price",
      "how much to pay for a used treadmill",
      "used treadmill value",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "See Used vs New Prices", link: "#price-table" }}
>
  <article class="ed-article" data-template="editorial">
    <div class="ed-col">
      <nav class="ed-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/price/">By Price</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        <span>Price Guide</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="ed-title">How Much Does a Used Treadmill Cost?</h1>
      <p class="ed-dek">
        It depends far more on who is selling than on the brand. On 25 November 2026 maker scratch-and-dent units were selling at about 87% of the new price, remanufactured gym treadmills cost $3,799 to $10,599 at one specialist dealer, and one resale marketplace put a typical used Peloton Tread sale at about $1,800. With Black Friday cutting new prices this week, a used home treadmill is only a bargain once moving, wear parts and the missing warranty are counted. Here are the dated pairs, the hidden costs and the sums.
      </p>

      <!-- Byline -->
      <div class="ed-byline">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="44" height="44" />
        <div class="ed-byline-text">
          By <a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a><br />
          Updated November 27, 2026 · Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS<br />
          <span class="ed-method">Based on retailer and maker listings, with prices checked on the dates shown.</span>
        </div>
        <a href="#price-table" class="btn-ghost">Used vs New Price Pairs</a>
      </div>
      <p class="ed-disclosure">
        Nothing on this page is a paid placement, and it carries no affiliate links. <a href="/editorial-standards/">How we review.</a>
      </p>

      <div class="ed-body prose prose-lg">
        <p class="ed-lead">
          There is no single used treadmill price, because &ldquo;used&rdquo; covers four very different purchases: a
          maker&rsquo;s own scratch-and-dent unit with a warranty, a gym machine rebuilt by a dealer, a machine sold
          through a brand&rsquo;s resale marketplace, and a stranger&rsquo;s treadmill in a basement. Each prices
          differently. This page sets out every used or refurbished price we could read from a seller&rsquo;s own site,
          beside the new price for the same machine, with the date on each. Where a figure could not be read we say so
          rather than guess, and we do not quote private-sale prices from local marketplaces, because those listings
          cannot be checked reliably. Instead we show you how to price-check one yourself.
        </p>

        <nav class="ed-toc not-prose" aria-label="On this page">
          <h2>On this page</h2>
          <ol>
            <li><a href="#short-answer">The Short Answer</a></li>
            <li><a href="#price-table">Used vs New Pairs</a></li>
            <li><a href="#by-channel">Prices by Seller</a></li>
            <li><a href="#price-check">Price-Check a Listing</a></li>
            <li><a href="#age-hours">Age and Hours</a></li>
            <li><a href="#hidden-costs">Hidden Costs</a></li>
            <li><a href="#common-models">Common Models</a></li>
            <li><a href="#new-on-sale">When New Wins</a></li>
            <li><a href="#negotiating">Negotiating and Paying Safely</a></li>
            <li><a href="#faq">Frequently asked questions</a></li>
          </ol>
        </nav>

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>The Short Answer</h2>
<p>
            <strong>A used treadmill costs whatever the nearest new equivalent costs on sale, minus what you lose by
            buying used: the warranty, free delivery and some of the machine&rsquo;s life. In the dated pairs we could
            find on 25 November 2026, maker scratch-and-dent units sold at about 87% of new, remanufactured commercial
            treadmills at about 43% to 59% of the new commercial price, and used Peloton treadmills at roughly half the
            list price of the models that replaced them.</strong> Those are separate markets, not one depreciation curve.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Maker scratch-and-dent:</strong> <a href="/sb-fitness-ct550-curved-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>SB Fitness CT550</a> $1,745 against $1,995 new; CT700 $2,245 against $2,595 (SB Fitness store, 14 Oct 2026).</li>
            <li><strong>Remanufactured gym treadmills:</strong> $3,799 to $10,599 for the 93 in-stock models at Fitness Superstore, median $4,099, with a 1-year parts and on-site labour warranty (25 Nov 2026).</li>
            <li><strong>Used Peloton Tread:</strong> typical sale about $1,800 (median $1,786) and median asking $2,157.50, per the resale marketplace Commonplace (August and 7 October 2026).</li>
            <li><strong>Private sale:</strong> no reliable figure exists; price it from the steps in our <a href="#price-check" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">price-check section</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>This week&rsquo;s alternative:</strong> new Black Friday prices such as the Horizon T101 at $784.40 and the Sole F80 at $1,499.99 set the ceiling a used home machine has to beat.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            For the wider decision, read our <a href="/new-vs-used-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">new
            vs used treadmill guide</a>; for where the machines turn up, see <a href="/where-to-buy-a-used-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">where to buy a used treadmill</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="price-table" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Used and Refurbished Prices Against New, Model by Model</h2>
<p>
            Every row below pairs a used, refurbished or second-quality price with a new price for the same machine, or,
            where the model is no longer sold new, with its direct replacement. The final column is simple division of
            the two figures shown, so you can see where the ratio comes from. We only included pairs where both numbers
            came from a seller&rsquo;s own page or a dated source already cited on this site.
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[720px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Machine</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Used or refurbished</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">New</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Source and date</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Used as % of new</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">SB Fitness CT550 (curved)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$1,745 scratch-and-dent</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$1,995</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">SB Fitness store, 14 Oct 2026</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">87%</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">SB Fitness CT700 (curved)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$2,245 scratch-and-dent</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$2,595</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">SB Fitness store, 14 Oct 2026</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">87%</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Star Trac 4 Series, 15-inch embedded display</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$4,999 remanufactured (2024 model)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$8,499</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Fitness Superstore, 25 Nov 2026</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">59%</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Star Trac 8 Series TR, 20-inch display</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$6,999 new out of box</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$13,649</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Fitness Superstore, 25 Nov 2026</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">51%</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Technogym Skillmill (curved)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$7,899 remanufactured</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$15,250</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Fitness Superstore, 25 Nov 2026; Technogym US store, 20 Oct 2026</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">52%</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Star Trac 10 Series FreeRunner</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$7,299 remanufactured, 19-inch display (shown out of stock)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$16,999 with 20-inch display</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Fitness Superstore, 25 Nov 2026</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">43% (consoles differ)</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Peloton Tread (original)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">About $1,800 typical sale</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Replacement Tread Vision $3,495 list</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Commonplace, Aug 2026; Peloton, 5 Nov 2026</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">52% of the replacement</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Peloton Tread+ (previous slat-belt model)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$2,990 median asking (5 listings)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Replacement Tread+ Vision $6,695 list</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Commonplace, 7 Oct 2026; Peloton, 5 Nov 2026</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">45% of the replacement</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            Three things stand out. First, a maker&rsquo;s cosmetic second is barely discounted: about 13% off, because
            it is mechanically new. Second, remanufactured commercial machines sell for roughly half to three-fifths of
            a new commercial price, but that is still more than almost any new home treadmill. Third, the Peloton
            figures compare old machines against the dearer models that replaced them on 1 October 2026; against the
            Black Friday <a href="/peloton-tread/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>Tread Vision</a> price of $2,795 (Peloton, 24 Nov 2026) the same $1,800 is 64%, which is why the
            sale matters so much.
          </p>
          <p>
            We could not read used or refurbished prices from NordicTrack, ProForm, Sole, Horizon, Bowflex, Johnson
            Fitness (Matrix, Horizon) or Life Fitness&rsquo;s own stores on 25 November: each returned a block or a
            rate-limit page. Amazon&rsquo;s product search returned no Renewed treadmills on the same day, only renewed
            spare parts such as control boards. Peloton Repowered&rsquo;s listings load in the browser and were not
            readable to us, so its individual asking prices are not shown.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="by-channel" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>What You Pay Depends on Who Is Selling</h2>
<p>
            The same treadmill can be worth very different sums depending on what the seller stands behind. These are
            the five channels, from most to least protected, with what each was charging or offering this month.
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[640px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead><tr><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Channel</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Price evidence</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Warranty and delivery</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Maker scratch-and-dent or open box</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">About 87% of new (SB Fitness, 14 Oct 2026)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Sold by the maker; ask what warranty applies to the second</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Remanufactured commercial (specialist dealer)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$3,799&ndash;$10,599, median $4,099 (Fitness Superstore, 25 Nov 2026)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">1-year parts and on-site labour; extended 2&ndash;5 years offered; free local delivery near Benicia, CA on $1,000+ orders, paid freight elsewhere</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Brand resale marketplace (Peloton Repowered)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Seller-set; listings not readable to us</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$95 activation fee waived; delivery through AptDeco at extra cost, or pickup</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Third-party resale marketplace</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Used Tread typical sale about $1,800 (Commonplace, Aug 2026)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Usually none; delivery extra</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Private sale (local listings)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Not quotable; check comparable listings yourself</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">None in practice; you collect it</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Maker seconds: small discount, low risk</h3>
          <p>
            A scratch-and-dent or open-box unit sold by the maker is a new machine with a mark on it. SB Fitness&rsquo;s
            two curved trainers show the pattern: $250 and $350 off machines costing $1,995 and $2,595. If a maker&rsquo;s
            own outlet offers one at that kind of discount, it is usually the safest way to pay less, but it is rarely a
            dramatic saving, and on a week like this one a full-price new machine on sale can undercut it. Our <a href="/refurbished-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">refurbished treadmills guide</a> explains what to ask before buying any second.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Remanufactured gym machines: cheaper than new commercial, dearer than new home</h3>
          <p>
            Fitness Superstore, a California dealer, listed 173 remanufactured treadmills on 25 November, 93 of them in
            stock. The in-stock prices started at $3,799 (models including the Life Fitness <a href="/life-fitness-95t-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>95Ti</a>, Precor C956i, Cybex
            525T and Landice L9) and ran to $10,599 for a Woodway 4Front with the Personal Trainer 2024 display; the median was $4,099.
            Its warranty page states a 1-year parts and on-site labour warranty on all remanufactured machines, with
            extensions of two to five years for sale, and the store was offering an extra 5% off remanufactured stock
            with a Black Friday code until 30 November. Compare that $3,799 floor with the new NordicTrack Commercial 1750
            at $1,999 on Amazon on the same day: a rebuilt club treadmill is a different class of machine, heavier and
            built for far more hours, but it is not the cheap option. Our <a href="/how-much-does-a-commercial-treadmill-cost/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">commercial treadmill cost guide</a> covers new club prices.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Peloton Repowered and resale marketplaces</h3>
          <p>
            Peloton&rsquo;s own resale site said on 25 November that it is available nationwide, with delivery in the
            contiguous states through AptDeco, that sellers set their own price and receive 70% of the sale, and that
            buyers there skip the $95 used-equipment activation fee a private-sale buyer would normally pay. It also
            gives buyers three days after delivery or pickup to report a problem. That is more protection than a private
            sale, but it is not a warranty. Our <a href="/used-peloton-tread/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">used
            Peloton Tread guide</a> covers the recall checks and account transfer.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Private sales</h3>
          <p>
            Local listings have the most machines and the lowest prices, and the least of everything else: no warranty,
            no delivery and no recourse. Asking prices there are set by the seller&rsquo;s memory of what they paid, not
            by the market, so the number on the listing tells you little. The next section shows how to work out what it
            is actually worth.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="price-check" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>How to Price-Check a Marketplace Listing</h2>
<p>
            We do not quote Facebook Marketplace or Craigslist prices, because listings change by the hour, many never
            sell at the asking price and none can be checked after the fact. You can still get to a sound number in about
            twenty minutes. Work through these steps in order.
          </p>
          <ol>
            <li><strong>Identify the exact model and year.</strong> Ask for a photo of the serial-number sticker, usually
            on the frame near the power switch or under the motor hood. &ldquo;NordicTrack treadmill&rdquo; covers machines
            from $445 to over $2,000 new.</li>
            <li><strong>Find the nearest new equivalent and its price today.</strong> If the model is still sold, use its
            current sale price, not its list price. If it has been replaced, use the replacement. This week, use the Black
            Friday figures in the table further down.</li>
            <li><strong>Look at sold prices, not asking prices.</strong> On eBay, filter a search for the model to sold
            items; on local marketplaces, note how long similar listings have stayed up. A listing that has been live for
            a month at the same price is over-priced.</li>
            <li><strong>Collect three to five comparable listings</strong> of the same or a similar model within a sensible
            driving distance, and note age, hours and condition for each.</li>
            <li><strong>Subtract your real costs</strong>: moving, any wear part you can already see needs replacing, and
            an allowance for having no warranty (the hidden-costs table below has dated part prices).</li>
            <li><strong>Check parts are still sold</strong> for that exact model. If you cannot find a belt or control board
            for it, the first fault ends the machine, and it is worth much less.</li>
          </ol>
          <p>
            The result is your ceiling, not your offer. Our <a href="/used-treadmill-buying-checklist/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">used treadmill buying checklist</a> lists the mechanical checks to make in person, and anything it turns up is a reason to offer less.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="age-hours" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>What Age and Hours Do to a Used Treadmill&rsquo;s Value</h2>
<p>
            We will not give you a percentage-per-year depreciation figure, because we could find no dated data set that
            supports one, and the pairs above show that the discount depends more on the channel than on the calendar.
            What we can say is which facts about age and use should move the price, and in which direction.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Age: how much life is left</h3>
          <p>
            A used treadmill&rsquo;s value is the useful life it has left. Our <a href="/how-long-do-treadmills-last/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmill lifespan guide</a> gives these working ranges, which depend heavily on whether the deck was lubricated:
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[520px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead><tr><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Tier (new price)</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Maintained</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Neglected</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Walking pads ($250&ndash;$600)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">3&ndash;5 years</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">2&ndash;3 years</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Budget ($400&ndash;$800)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">5&ndash;8 years</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">2&ndash;4 years</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Mid-range ($800&ndash;$1,500)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">8&ndash;12 years</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">4&ndash;6 years</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Premium ($1,500&ndash;$2,500)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">10&ndash;15 years</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">5&ndash;8 years</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Commercial ($2,500+)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">15&ndash;20 years</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">8&ndash;12 years</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            The practical reading: a three-year-old walking pad or budget folder may have used most of its life, so it
            is worth little whatever its owner paid. A three-year-old premium or commercial machine can have most of its
            life ahead of it, which is why rebuilt club treadmills hold their prices so well.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Hours and distance</h3>
          <p>
            Most consoles store total hours or miles somewhere in a maintenance menu. Our checklist treats under 500 hours
            on a home machine as light use and over 1,500 hours as approaching mid-life, while 3,000 hours on a
            commercial-grade machine is not alarming. High miles with modest hours means it was run on rather than walked
            on, which is harder on the motor, belt and deck. Hours matter less than lubrication: a dry deck wears the belt
            and loads the motor and control board, so ask when it was last lubricated, and price a vague answer as a belt
            replacement.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Generation and software</h3>
          <p>
            Age also matters when a model has been replaced. Peloton swapped its whole treadmill range on 1 October 2026,
            and our Peloton guide notes that this should push used asking prices down; Commonplace&rsquo;s August sale
            figure predates it. Smart treadmills also depend on the maker&rsquo;s app and subscription: a console that can
            no longer update, or a machine still tied to the seller&rsquo;s account, is worth less than one that activates
            cleanly in your name.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Warranty</h3>
          <p>
            Many home-treadmill warranties cover the original purchaser only, so unless the maker confirms in writing that
            cover transfers, price a private-sale machine as having none. A <a href="/best-treadmills-with-long-warranty/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>lifetime motor warranty</a> on a listing, such as
            the one in the Horizon T101 Connect&rsquo;s Amazon title, is worth a great deal to the first owner and may be
            worth nothing to you.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="hidden-costs" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>The Hidden Costs of a Used Treadmill</h2>
<p>
            The asking price is only the start. These are the costs a new machine bought on sale usually does not carry,
            with dated prices where a seller published one.
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[640px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead><tr><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Cost</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Price</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Source and date</th></tr></thead>
