              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Warranty</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">None on most private sales</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Remanufactured dealer stock is the exception (1 year at Fitness Superstore)</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Moving</h3>
          <p>
            This is the cost that most often wipes out the saving. A full-size treadmill rarely fits in a car, and the
            heavy non-folding machines that make the best used buys are the hardest to move: Peloton&rsquo;s figures put
            the current Tread Flex at 290 lb and the Tread+ Vision at 460 lb. If you can borrow a van and two strong
            helpers, collection is nearly free; if not, budget for a mover who charges for stairs and distance. New
            machines often include curbside delivery, and Bowflex&rsquo;s Black Friday offer on the T16 included free
            shipping, against a normal $99 standard delivery charge (Bowflex, 24 Nov 2026). Our <a href="/how-to-move-a-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">guide
            to moving a treadmill</a> and the <a href="/treadmill-delivery-guide/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmill
            delivery guide</a> cover both routes.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Belt and lubrication</h3>
          <p>
            Budget a bottle of silicone lubricant for any used machine, and a belt if the old one is frayed, glazed or the
            seller cannot say when the deck was last lubricated. At $97 to $140 for a third-party belt it is not ruinous,
            but it should come off your offer. Our <a href="/treadmill-belt-replacement-cost/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">belt replacement cost guide</a> covers fitting it yourself versus paying a technician.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">The expensive unknowns</h3>
          <p>
            The motor and control board are what you cannot see. A replacement board ran $108 to $289 on Amazon this
            week before labour, and a board fault often follows years of running on a dry deck. That risk is what a
            warranty covers on a new machine, and why a private-sale price has to sit well below a new one.
          </p>
        </div>

